& [Observation] is unconstrained adapter concurrency
  + MCP server handlers may overlap and the server is cloneable
  + each accepted route_attention call launches a separate Needle controller process
  + simultaneous jobs can compete for accelerator memory CPU evidence paths and latency budget even though each individual child is bounded

& [Intent] is one explicit process-local execution token
  + exactly one route call may own the token at a time
  + a competing call fails immediately with typed runtime_busy and launches no child
  + no hidden queue order retry priority or fairness claim is introduced
  + permit release is automatic on success refusal verification failure timeout cancellation or panic unwinding
  + startup health occurs before the server opens and does not require the runtime token

& [Boundary] is process-local resource admission
  + it is not shared inference negotiation distributed locking or semantic authority
  + multiple independently launched adapter processes still require an operator-level singleton or exterior scheduler

& [Deferred] includes bounded queues priorities distributed leases token rings and multi-host arbitration
